/*
 * COM_DATA.C  the computer player's tuning data
 *
 * Most tables are indexed by character number and CPU level: the attack and shell ranges of
 * each character (Area_Unit_Data, Shell_Area_Unit_Data, Dash_Distance_Data,
 * PL_Body_Width_Data), combo speed and reaction times, wait times, guard, parry and
 * throw-escape chances (Guard_Data, Flip_Data, Exit_Throw_Data and the rest), and the opponent
 * move and range lists the checks test against. Read by COM_PL.C, COM_SUB.C and CK_PASS.C.
 * Com_Vital_Unit_Data gives the starting vitality by character, damage setting and level
 * (PLSGAUGE.C); Correct_Cont_Time_Data and Demo_Lever_Data the select-screen time cut after
 * continues and the demo lever input (SEL_PL.C); Middle_Class_Boss_Data and
 * Combo_Demo_Lever_Data the mid boss of each character and the combo demo input (EM_CAND.C);
 * Boss_Speech_Data whether the boss speech plays before the last two opponents (NEXT_CPU.C).
 * Shell_Area_Step_Data and Passive_Guard_Off_Data are not referred to by name.
 */

